  "synopsis": [
    {
      "langue": "en",
      "text": "Nagagutsu o Haita Neko: Sekai Issh 80 Nichi Dai Boken (lit. &quot;Puss in Boots: An Adventure Around the World in 80 Days&quot;) is a video game based on the third film of The Wonderful World of Puss 'n Boots that was released exclusively in Japan for the Family Computer. Four years later, the game (with several modifications) was released in North America under the title Puss 'n Boots: Pero's Great Adventure.\r\nPero has to either avoid or eliminate this cat-like enemies who stands in his way. The main character is the Puss in Boots character from the tale; a cat named Pero (Toei Animation's mascot) He is also known as 'Perrault' in the game, as that was the name of the original author of the Puss In Boots story; Charles Perrault. He is known for helping an impoverished master attain wealth through the use of trickery.\r\nLoosely based on Jules Verne's classic novel Around the World in Eighty Days tied together with a classic anime, the player has 80 days in order to travel the world; this is shown through a time limit. One day passes in the game approximately every minute, although certain items can subtract the number of remaining days, providing the player with less time to complete the game. If these 80 days elapse before the player finishes the trip, the game is over no matter how many lives the player has remaining. Places that are explored include: England, the Atlantic Ocean, Arabia, Hong Kong, the Pacific Ocean, Alaska, the North Pole, and Big Ben. The game features &quot;death water,&quot; a video game feature where video game characters instantly die after coming into contact with a watery substance.\r\nThis game also involves driving boats, cars, and balloons in addition to the standard walking through the stages."
    },
    {
      "langue": "fr",
      "text": "Jeu video sorti en 1986 exclusivement au japon, puis adapté 4 ans plus tard en Amérique du Nord sous le titre &quot;Puss'n Boots Pero's Great Adventure&quot; mais avec de nombreuses modifications (level design, boss, head-up display) \r\nJeu basé sur un roman de Jules Vernes (le monde en 80 jours) , le personnage principal Pero (un chat surement prénommé ainsi d'apres l'auteur du du Chat botté, Charles Perrault) doit parcourir le monde en moins de 80 jours, sur son chemin il aura des monstres à vaincre. La particularité du jeu c'est que 1 min dans le jeu correspond à 1 jour, si le décompte arrive à son terme et que le joueur n'a pas fini de parcourir les différents pays la partie est terminée."
    },
    {
      "langue": "de",
      "text": "Das Videospiel wurde 1986 ausschließlich in Japan veröffentlicht und 4 Jahre später in Nordamerika unter dem Titel „Der gestiefelte Kater Pero's Great Adventure“ adaptiert, jedoch mit zahlreichen Modifikationen (Leveldesign, Boss, Head-up-Display).\r\nSpiel basierend auf einem Roman von Jules Vernes (Die Welt in 80 Tagen). Die Hauptfigur Pero (eine Katze, die wahrscheinlich nach dem Autor von Der gestiefelte Kater, Charles Perrault, benannt wurde) muss die Welt in weniger als 80 Tagen bereisen wird Monster zu besiegen haben. Die Besonderheit des Spiels besteht darin, dass 1 Minute im Spiel einem Tag entspricht. Wenn der Countdown abgelaufen ist und der Spieler die Reise durch die verschiedenen Länder noch nicht beendet hat, ist das Spiel vorbei."
    },
    {
      "langue": "es",
      "text": "Videojuego lanzado en 1986 exclusivamente en Japón, luego se adaptó 4 años más tarde en América del Norte con el título &quot;Puss'n Boots Pero's Great Adventure&quot;, pero con muchas modificaciones (diseño de niveles, jefe, pantalla de visualización). Juego basado en una novela de Jules Vernes (el mundo en 80 días), el personaje principal Pero (un gato seguramente nombrado por el autor del Gato con botas, Charles Perrault) debe viajar por el mundo en menos de 80 días, en su camino Tendrá monstruos para derrotar. La peculiaridad del juego es que 1 minuto en el juego es 1 día, si el conteo llega a su fin y el jugador no ha terminado de navegar por los diferentes países, el juego terminó."
    },
    {
      "langue": "it",
      "text": "Videogioco uscito nel 1986 esclusivamente in Giappone, poi adattato 4 anni dopo in Nord America con il titolo &quot;Il gatto e gli stivali Pero's Great Adventure&quot; ma con molte modifiche (design dei livelli, boss, head-up display)\r\nGioco basato su un romanzo di Jules Vernes (il mondo in 80 giorni), il protagonista Pero (un gatto probabilmente intitolato all'autore del gatto con gli stivali, Charles Perrault) deve girare il mondo in meno di 80 giorni, per la sua strada avrà mostri da sconfiggere. La particolarità del gioco è che 1 min di gioco corrisponde a 1 giorno, se il conto alla rovescia giunge al termine e il giocatore non ha finito di viaggiare attraverso i diversi paesi, il gioco è terminato."
    },
    {
      "langue": "pt",
      "text": "Videogame lançado em 1986 exclusivamente no Japão e adaptado 4 anos depois na América do Norte sob o título &quot;A Grande Aventura de Puss'n Boots Pero&quot;, mas com muitas modificações (design de níveis, chefe, display head-up)\r\nJogo baseado em um romance de Jules Vernes (o mundo em 80 dias), o personagem principal Pero (um gato provavelmente assim batizado em homenagem ao autor de Gato de Botas, Charles Perrault) deve viajar o mundo em menos de 80 dias, em seu caminho ele terá monstros para derrotar. A particularidade do jogo é que 1 min de jogo corresponde a 1 dia, se a contagem terminar e o jogador não terminar de navegar pelos diferentes países o jogo acaba."
    }
  ],
